.TH ZERODDS-ZENOH-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-zenoh-bridged \- DDS to Eclipse Zenoh bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-zenoh-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIpeer\fR|\fIclient\fR|\fIrouter\fR]
[\fB\-\-connect\fR \fIENDPOINT\fR]...
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIENDPOINT\fR]...
[\fB\-\-no\-multicast\-scouting\fR]
[\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIDDS\fR[\fI:DIR\fR]]...
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-zenoh-bridged
bridges DDS topics and Eclipse Zenoh key expressions in both directions. It
is wire-compatible with Zenoh's own DDS bridge,
.RB ( zenoh\-plugin\-dds " / " zenoh\-bridge\-dds ,
github.com/eclipse-zenoh/zenoh-plugin-dds):
the default key-expression layout
.RI ( <scope>/<partition>/<topic> ,
scope empty by default), the Zenoh payload (the full RTPS-encapsulated CDR
blob, not the header-stripped body), the
.BR reliable_routes_blocking -driven
.B CongestionControl
choice and the TRANSIENT_LOCAL late-joiner mechanism
.RI ( PublicationCache / FetchingSubscriber )
all match the plugin's, so a
.B zerodds-zenoh-bridged
on one site and a
.B zenoh-bridge-dds
on another interoperate on the same Zenoh network. See
.I crates/zenoh-bridge/src/mapping.rs
for the exact source citations this crate was read against.
.PP
Every DDS topic the daemon discovers (via the DCPS built-in topics) is
bridged automatically, filtered by
.BR discovery.allow / deny ,
the way
.B zenoh-plugin-dds
bridges every topic it sees; topics can also be listed explicitly under
.B topics:
for QoS overrides, an explicit key-expression, or a
.B type_file
(needed for a keyed topic bridged Zenoh\(->DDS, to derive the real
per-instance key hash instead of collapsing every instance onto one).
.PP
.B zenoh-plugin-dds
does not forward DDS dispose/unregister in either direction (it silently
skips them). This project's rule against dropping a sample without a trace
means
.B zerodds-zenoh-bridged
does forward dispose/unregister, as a Zenoh
.B delete
on
.IR <key-expr>/<key-hash-hex> ,
an extension of the plugin's key layout, not a replacement for it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
YAML config. See
.BR zerodds-zenoh-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-mode =\fIpeer\fR|\fIclient\fR|\fIrouter\fR
Zenoh session mode. Default:
.IR peer .
.TP
.BR \-\-connect =\fIENDPOINT\fR
Zenoh endpoint to connect to, e.g.
.IR tcp/192.0.2.10:7447
(repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIENDPOINT\fR
Zenoh endpoint to listen on (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-multicast\-scouting
Disable Zenoh's UDP multicast scouting (matches
.B zenoh-bridge-dds
\&'s own flag of the same name).
.TP
.BR \-\-scope =\fISCOPE\fR
Zenoh key-expression scope. Default: none (matching
.BR zenoh-plugin-dds ).
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIDDS\fR[\fI:DIR\fR]
Topic override, DIR one of
.IR in ", " out ", " bidir
(repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the daemon: every forward pump joins and every Zenoh
subscriber/publication cache is undeclared before exit.
SIGHUP reads the configuration again:
.BR discovery.allow / deny / auto_bridge
apply to the poll iterations that follow. A changed
.BR domain ,
.BR zenoh. \fI* \fR,
or
.B topics:
needs a restart (the Zenoh session and the registered DDS readers/writers
are not torn down and rebuilt on reload) and is logged, not applied. A
configuration that does not load changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Bind error: a metrics or admin listen address is already in use.
.TP
.B 3
DDS discovery error.
.TP
.B 4
Zenoh session error.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/zenoh-bridged.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-zenoh-bridged.yaml (5).
